{"name":"Canadian Pancake","hex":"#edd8c3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pancake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thin batter cake fried in a pan or on a griddle in oil or butter; in particular:\n An thin batter cake similar to a crepe, typically unleavened.\n A leavened, thicker, fluffier cake.","An thin batter cake similar to a crepe, typically unleavened."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a pancake landing.","To collapse one floor after another."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pancake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canadians","blocks":[{"text":"Canadians are people identified with the country of Canada. This connection may be residential, legal, historical or cultural. For most Canadians, many of these connections exist and are collectively the source of their being Canadian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_Canada_%28Pantone%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadians"},{"title":"Pancake","blocks":[{"text":"A pancake, also known as a hotcake, griddlecake, or flapjack, is a flat type of batter bread like cake, often thin and round, prepared from a starch-based batter that may contain eggs, milk, and butter, and then cooked on a hot surface such as a griddle or frying pan. Archaeological evidence suggests that pancakes were probably eaten in prehistoric societies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Foodiesfeed.com_pouring-honey-on-pancakes-with-walnuts.jpg/330px-Foodiesfeed.com_pouring-honey-on-pancakes-with-walnuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pancake"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Outside_Union_Station.jpg/500px-Outside_Union_Station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai